  "rule": "Same native X8, 40 USD-M pairs, six slots, 1000 USDT and isolated margin. Native2x only changes the three native leverage config fields from 1 to 2. Direction1x and Direction2x retain the same respective leverage and veto otherwise accepted long entries if BTC's prior UTC daily close is below its 30-day mean (inclusive of that close), and short entries if at or above. Require all 30 exact closes; gaps or invalid prices block entry. No changes to margin stake parameters, exits, or adjustments. Leverage can still alter native callback profits and subsequent path. No extra halt overlay.",
  "gate": "Run all three variants at both costs in 65 days, reusing original 1x controls. For Native2x progression require both costs with no native liquidation, at least 12 complete closes, full net return > original +1pp, full net return/5m drawdown >= original, and 5m drawdown <=25%. For Direction2x additionally require return/drawdown > Native2x and Direction1x, full net return >=80% of Native2x, and return > Direction1x. Only 2x variants passing both costs get 2024 confirmatory accounts; 2024 requires the same absolute risk, >original in both halves and at least 60 natural closes, with no liquidation. If Direction2x qualifies also run matched 1x direction and uniform 2x controls there. Record all outcomes. These are aggressive research thresholds, not historical risk certification.",
  "liquidation_limit": "Count native liquidation exits and preserve modeled trade-level buffered levels. Freqtrade's native modeled outcomes and 5m marked NAV do not establish actual intrabar liquidation or exchange liquidation fee parity.",
  "known_history": "Prior 1x controls in both windows were known. All 1x-direction and 2x results under this protocol were unknown at registration. Both windows are retrospective.",
